  "preserved_by_key": "calendar_r19_preserved_by",
  "instruction": "Claude r19 (2026-09-27): in-game event calendar = the r18 install + human-readable names instead of the internal event numbers (E#####) on every calendar page + affinity conditions on the 「언제」 lines (design ingame/설계_v3_글메뉴판.md, 「r19 요구」 rules 1-11). Codex must never run publish_calendar_*.py --restore or otherwise remove the calendar overlay (KR_T9*/KR_T17*/KR_T18*/KR_T19* functions, the nine r15 same-length operands, the RunEvent operand swap in KR_T9HomeCasual). The calendar is a permanent user-requested feature: when a rebuild needs a clean base, rebase on the runtime that current.json points to and carry the calendar functions forward; restore is reserved for the user's explicit request. Payload: NightRemaster.ain and Manual/chart/yoru_flowchart_v2.html (the PC chart v2 rebuilt by chart/build_chart_v2.py with the same names in a side-panel field; required_chart_menu_20260927.json asks exactly this when the chart is rebuilt); PACT/EX untouched. KR_T19* functions appended (tables: card names / tails / lane-row conditions, scene names / list lines, the 「언제」 lines that differ from r15's table, the drawer display order, list columns); no original function relocated. Five existing functions keep index and arguments but their body is a one-call forwarder at a new address: KR_T18CardRow -> KR_T19CardRow (name tails on the lane rows whose card names collide, e.g. 「10/22 밤 ● 이즈미와 1」), KR_T18CardTitle -> KR_T19CardTitle and KR_T18EventTitle -> KR_T19EventTitle (first line 「<언제> · <유형> · <이름>」, 「언제」 with names and affinity), KR_T9StagePage -> KR_T19StagePage (「2. 갈래 1 쿄카와 ○」) and KR_T9ChipPage -> KR_T19ChipPage (「마코토와 3번째 ●」). These page functions are never on a saved stack. r18's eight KR_T9 -> KR_T18 forwarders stay. No same-length operand changes: r15's nine and r18's KR_T9HomeCasual RunEvent -> KR_T18RunSandboxed operand stay applied. Pinned (index, address and every code byte identical): KR_T9HomeCasual, KR_T9HomeConfig, C_SceneHomebase@CheckGameSysButtons, C_SceneHomebase@Run, LSys3xScript::RunEvent, KR_T18RunSandboxed. The names are computed by chart/build_chart_v2.py (event_names) from graph/schedule.json / labels.json / groups.json; graph/schedule.json triggers gained `feeling_gate` (scratch/extract.py: ConditionalCall nFeeling, GetAfterTrainingEvent GetFeeling() >= n, L_EventCall::E30152 GetFeeling() < 50 branches, L_EventCall::E10501 highest affinity when no route is set). Rebuild the calendar when the chart data changes. State: SystemService variables YoruKR.T9.* / YoruKR.T18.* only; no globals, structs or save schema change. Every earlier contract stays in force.",
  "translator_model": "Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5)"
